**Py'rah** (/'*pɛɪraː*/, *[[shadow-cant|Shadow Cant]]*: ꔪꕟ, [[ukrashan|Ukrashan]]: *𐒋𐒜𐒘𐒇𐒛*, romanized: Thyra) is one of the seven elemental deities. He is bound to the element of Darkness and he is the god of death and madness. Worship of Py'rah has been outlawed since the [[decemvir-era|Decemvir Era]] and no adjustments have been made after [[sorrows-dawn|Sorrow's Dawn]].

-----
# Religion
The Pyran religion is a hidden banned religion having been forced to take place in secret. The Vai%%Vai is a mention to the shadow cant alphabet being taken from the Vai language%% on the rare occasion the commune, meet in a hidden location. Like caves, hideouts and abandoned churches. Otherwise they have personal shrines covered up in their residences. They often include symbolism in the form of the *Der'gulas cross*[^dc] and the Sigil of Pyrah. The Pyran religion has adjusted heavily since its ban in the [[decemvir-era|Decemvir Era]] and the religious symbols which were heavily prevalent back them, have completely dissipated from public view. Many other smaller deities have filled the void left behind by the ban of this elemental deity.

Their commune is appropriately named a Black Mass. They make their way to a secret location and wear all black and a form of mask. These outfits are the predominant evidence of a Vai. They light candles and say prayers in a stoic ritual.

The *Illud Mortis*[^im] is the most protected relic of the Vai, they are very secretive of it's location, most people are unsure of its existence. If it would end up int he hand of another religious figure head would be devastating to the power of the domains. These words are the only remnants left from Py'rah pre-ascension.

The story of Py'rah ascension is one of the many stories written in the Illud Mortis. It describes how he conquered three smaller deities to become a elemental deity. He conquered the God of Death, *Nimrod*[^nimrod], the God of Trickery, *Thuden*[^thuden] and the God of Darkness, *Dhiznir*[^dhiznir]. The exquisite details of these battles are described, but no words describe the way ha gained the ability to fight the gods. The combined power of these three domain forged an connection to the element of Darkness for the first time. This element had been empty ever since the appearance of the elemental domains.
## Sects
%%The 'founder' of satanism was LaVey%%
- Vey of **Thanathos**[^thanathos]
Thanathos is the Vey focused on the Underworld and it's Demons. They believe in the rise of the demons, and their salvation. 
- Vey of **Margos**[^margos]
Margos is the chaos turned Vey. They once had a different set of beliefs, but turned mad at a point in time. They have secluded themselves and live in a pseudo reality.
- Vey of **Aither**[^aither]
Aither is the Vey of outcasts. They are the people on who the world turned its back, but the devil himself extended his hand. Their relationship with Py'rah is more equal compared to others. They have learned the art of deception in their practices.
- Vey of **Nyx**[^nyx]
The Vey of Nyx are the worshipers of the Night. They are as close to nocturnal as they can reasonably be. They are weary of the sun, fire and anything else related tot he daytime.

## Structure
### Venerated Ancestors
*See also: [[list-of-pyran-venerated-ancestors|List of Pyran Venerated Ancestors]]*
The venerated ancestors from the Pyran religion doesn't hold any value in other religions anymore. They would had to have commit acts considered to be holy by the Vai, most of them have been honored in legends. They are addressed with the Prefix *Olu*[^olu] or *Oluwa*[^oluwa], bestowed upon them posthumously.

### Priestly Order
The communion of the Pyran religion is communal, as responsibility is shared among them. Yet a leader is a appointed, they are supposed to delegate the communion and are addressed by the *Gaarozi*[^gaarozi] prefix.

# Cultural
## Illud Mortis
The *Illud Mortis*[^im] is the holy book of Py'rah. It is claimed as being the words of Py'rah himself. It appeared to a priest of Py'rah after he found the book in a remnants of battle. The book had previously held different words, but during battle it was covered in blood and torched. The priest could feel the power coming form this book and opened to discovered that the burning revealed words in the blood covered pages.

## Shadow Cant / Loavada
*See also: [[shadow-cant|Shadow Cant]]*
Shadow Cant, or *Loavada*[^loavada], is the secret form of communication revived by the Vai. They use a script from a extinct language and they constructed a new form of grammar. Shadow cant's primary purpose is for secret communication between the Vai.

## Aeonian Eclipse
The Aeonian Eclipse is the holy day of Py'rah, it marks the anniversary of his ascension. The day contains three communes for the Vai, each one marking a victory in battle and the conquest of domain. In between it is a feast with traditionally: beautifully cooked meats and blood red wine.

## Inquisition Penumbral[^ip]
*See also: Inquisition Penumbral*
The Inquisition Penumbral is the opposition of the Vai. After the outlawing of the worship of Py'rah, they set up a hunt for followers. As in most part of the worlds, such worship is punishable by death and the captor is granted a great boon. As such they form a international coalition of assassins, hunters and warriors constantly chasing the Vai.

